html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en-GB"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>United Kingdom · FLORA simplified design study</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="refined.css"><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to landscape</a><header><a class="brand" href="../index.html">FLORA</a><nav aria-label="Product"><a href="#main" aria-current="page">Explore</a><a href="#news">News</a><a href="#signals">Signals</a><a href="#opportunities">Opportunities</a><a href="#pipeline">Pipeline</a></nav><span class="role">Strategic Sales</span></header><main id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="title"><h1>United Kingdom</h1></div><figure class="world" aria-labelledby="description"><figcaption id="description" class="sr-only">Conceptual UK industry landscape. All 20 original industry labels remain at their original image-relative anchors. Only Banking, Technology and Aviation open researched destinations. Building size does not represent economic scale. On phones the same left and right halves stack.</figcaption>{scene}</figure><details class="deeper"><summary>Explore deeper</summary><div><a href="../a-government.html">Government</a><a href="#forces">Forces of Change</a><details id="forces"><summary>Forces of Change</summary><p>The existing six-factor PESTLE method and UK intelligence remain unchanged.</p></details><details><summary>About these figures and sources</summary><p>UK GVA, £2,623bn rounded to £2.62tn, 2024, GBP at current basic prices. Frozen existing ONS presentation extract, not a new source verification, GDP, revenue or sales market. Industry labels represent SIC 2007 sections; researched Banking, Technology and Aviation do not claim the whole host section. All original section shares and real GDP references remain in the existing baseline source disclosure. The stored rounded weights sum to 1,002 per thousand; source-note discrepancy is preserved for #607. No figures or research are changed.</p>{sources}</details><details id="aviation"><summary>Aviation</summary><p>The existing researched Aviation destination remains /industries/aviation. This design pack does not implement its page.</p></details><details><summary>Enterprises and connected actors</summary><a href="../a-banking.html">Banking landscape</a><a href="../a-technology.html">Technology landscape</a><p>Existing A detail studies are retained for reference, not accepted designs. Actor names, direction, identity, source scope and rights require existing evidence; no new relationship is inferred by these links.</p></details>'''
